WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.740
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:11.520
Today we are going to torment DeepMind’s&nbsp;
new AI called Ada with tasks that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.380
impossible. Kind of. And then, see&nbsp;
if it is smart enough to solve them.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:22.200
Now, you see, we talked about previous AI&nbsp;
techniques that were able to learn over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.300
time. For instance, NVIDIA’s little&nbsp;
knights were able to learn to fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:34.500
by themselves. But this took 10 years&nbsp;
of training. Not 10 years in our lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:40.740
10 years in their lives as they live inside&nbsp;
a simulation, which, with a quick computer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:47.100
will only take a few days to simulate.
In a different paper, AI agents started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:54.660
out like this. And over time, they learned to play&nbsp;
football and some really advanced techniques. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:02.880
there was no referee, so they also learned&nbsp;
to be not too kind to each other. Ouch. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:09.420
how long did this take? Well, these folks also&nbsp;
trained for years, in simulation time that is.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:15.840
And now, with DeepMind’s new AI, this agent&nbsp;
will hopefully be able learn cool new things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:22.440
and hopefully it will not take years. Yes,&nbsp;
we are going to build a virtual playhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.160
and play a little game. Throughout the game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:32.220
this little window to the world is what&nbsp;
the AI sees. Only we see the whole level.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:39.720
So now, little AI, you have one job. And&nbsp;
that is, to hold the black cube. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:47.700
there is a problem. What is the problem? Well, of&nbsp;
course, the fact that there is no black cube! Not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:55.680
one in sight. But we have a secret. The secret&nbsp;
is that if we touch the black pyramid with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:04.440
yellow sphere, out comes a black cube. However,&nbsp;
psst, this is a secret. The AI does not know about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:12.240
this rule and has to find out by itself. And&nbsp;
you know what, let’s make it even worse. If it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:18.900
touches the yellow sphere to the purple pyramid,&nbsp;
both get destroyed, making this task impossible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:27.360
to finish. And you know what, let’s make it even&nbsp;
worse. Give it a strict 20 second time limit. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:34.440
good luck with that, little AI! I can’t wait&nbsp;
to see this. This is going to be a lot of fun.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:41.460
So, let’s see. Round 1. It starts&nbsp;
exploring, likely to find the black cube,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:48.780
picks up the yellow sphere, dashes&nbsp;
away, and…oh boy! Bad news. Real bad.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:55.080
It proceeds to touch the purple pyramid,&nbsp;
you know what that means, right? Oh yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.080 --> 00:03:01.740
both of them get destroyed. Little does&nbsp;
the AI know, the task is now impossible.

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:07.020
It still tries to combine some objects&nbsp;
together, maybe something good happens,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:13.500
but we already know. Nothing good happens&nbsp;
here. And then, the time runs out.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:20.040
Now comes the interesting part. Did&nbsp;
it learn anything from this? I am so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:27.240
excited! Let’s start again! Hmm…it says&nbsp;
let’s not do what we did earlier. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:34.260
a good start. It takes the black pyramid, and,&nbsp;
there we go! Good job! We got the black cube,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:39.120
and now it is time…for a victory dance! Fantastic.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:47.220
So, is there any point in running round 3? Oh&nbsp;
yes. Yes there is! The goal is that we wish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:53.880
to see what it learned from the previous&nbsp;
success. Did it do it just by chance? Does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.880 --> 00:04:00.780
it really understand what just happened? Let’s&nbsp;
see. Oh boy! It is going straight for the correct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:07.080
answer. It really knows what just happened.&nbsp;
It truly uncovered the rules of this game,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.000
and now it is busy optimizing its&nbsp;
route to solve it even quicker.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:20.220
I love it. And when running a similar task for two&nbsp;
of these Ada agents, they learn the rules of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:29.700
game independently, but that is expected. However,&nbsp;
what is not expected is…look at that! Wow. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:36.480
learned to throw to get this task done quicker,&nbsp;
and later on, they even learned to work together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:44.280
to be even more efficient. So now, yes, it is time&nbsp;
to hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:51.120
what you are seeing here is learning happening&nbsp;
not in years, but in a matter of seconds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:58.560
Learning is so quick here, it is happening&nbsp;
right before our eyes. I can’t believe it.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:07.020
So if we can’t believe this, what do we do? Of&nbsp;
course, we make the task even more difficult. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.980
previous task could only be solved by lifting&nbsp;
things. So how about creating a level where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:21.540
lifting things make you lose immediately? That&nbsp;
sounds fun, right? This new level can only be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:29.940
solved by pushing. Of course, the AI does not know&nbsp;
that, so in round 1, it starts out lifting with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:37.560
predictable results. This was not a success.&nbsp;
So let’s see what has it learned? Round 2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:49.380
Look, it starts pushing instead. And when pushing&nbsp;
the two cubes together, got ‘em! Good job. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:55.320
was super quick learning. Once again, the&nbsp;
learning happened right before our eyes.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:06:03.240
So, what do we do now? Of course, we make it&nbsp;
even harder. Let’s add a bunch of unnecessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:09.780
rules and a ton of objects to distract the&nbsp;
AI from finding the yellow pyramid. Which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:17.400
by the way, doesn’t even exist. Yet. See if&nbsp;
it can see through our little tricks. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:25.320
some exploration happens, and transmutation also&nbsp;
happens. A lot of it. Something touches something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:32.880
and some other something appears. This doesn’t&nbsp;
even seem to make any sense. Note once again that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:39.660
only we see these rules and the whole map. The&nbsp;
AI does not know anything about the rules and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:46.920
playing this game for the first time, and only&nbsp;
sees this tiny window to the world. And later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.340
my goodness, look at that! With a stylish move,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.340 --> 00:07:00.420
it chucks away the yellow box that is in the&nbsp;
way. Fabulous! Then it holds the purple box,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:08.640
so what happens then? Look at the rules, yes, it&nbsp;
makes the highly coveted yellow pyramid appear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:17.040
Great! Then, it goes straight for the goal.&nbsp;
Learning is happening here too…and super quickly!

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:23.700
And in a different cooperative level, each player&nbsp;
has to touch their corresponding sphere to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:29.880
their pyramids, and when these new pyramids&nbsp;
touch, we are finished. For the first try,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:37.740
they try to explore and eventually succeed. But&nbsp;
do they really know how they succeeded? Do they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:45.840
know which actions were the ones responsible&nbsp;
for their success? Wow. For only the second try,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:53.400
they absolutely smashed it. That is just about&nbsp;
the quickest and most effective solution that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.400 --> 00:08:00.360
I can imagine. Holy mother of papers. This&nbsp;
little AI is learning incredibly quickly.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:06.300
And I have to be honest, when reading the&nbsp;
paper, I was a little worried if it could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:13.320
learn at all. Why? Well, because it is not&nbsp;
getting any intermediate rewards. What does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:19.380
that mean? It means that this game is a cruel&nbsp;
teacher that does not tell the AI during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:26.040
game how well it is doing. Only when it won&nbsp;
the level does it tell the AI so. Before that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:33.720
no information is given to the AI whether it is&nbsp;
doing well or poorly. This is especially difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:39.540
if we need to perform a chain of actions&nbsp;
to win the level, like you see here. And,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:47.580
my goodness, I am absolutely stunned that the AI&nbsp;
can still do it at all, let alone this quickly.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:57.180
So, in just one paper, we went from learning in a&nbsp;
matter of years to a matter of seconds. Wow. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:03.900
truly feels like seeing history in the making in&nbsp;
artificial intelligence. What a time to be alive!

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:09.780
So, what do you think? What would you use&nbsp;
this for? Let me know in the comments below!

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.400
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

